good-fortran is a translation of the computational portions of the R package "good" version 1.0.2.

Original package authors:
Jordi Tur, Amanda Fernandez-Fontelo, David Morina, Pere Puig, Argimiro Arratia, Alejandra Cabana, and David Agis.

Original package title: Good Regression
Original license: GPL (>= 2)
Original publication date in DESCRIPTION: 2024-05-17

This translation preserves the GPL-2.0-or-later licensing requirement. The original DESCRIPTION and NAMESPACE are retained under original/ for attribution and provenance.

The numerical implementation was rewritten in modern Fortran. R-specific formula parsing, S3 methods, printing, data frames, and dataset-loading infrastructure were intentionally omitted. No plotting code exists in the source package.
